A||||3||Ed||Electric door locks fixed: now this!||||3||
Z||000000||Ed||01-04-2000||11:47 PM||||Well, the lubrication of the electric door locks was "a piece of cake" as described on a previous thread. But now this! I found two "broken off" plastic fasteners, one in each door.  I replaced them with the generic fasteners as directed earlier on this board. <P>Maybe they weren't broken.  Today I guess was the first day I ran the windows down, because today they would go almost all the way down and then clunk; they were sticking on something. It dawned on me the fasteners may have been cut off to clear the lowered window. Since its not an emergency, I'm going to wait until the weekend to attack the problem.<P>Can anyone verify this as the probable cause of the windows hanging up?||||reg||3
Z||000001||deceler8||01-05-2000||07:41 PM||||I had the same problem with the manual windows on my '86 2m4...they would go almost all the way down and then hit a restriction.<P>I took wire cutters and cut off the end of the trim clip closest to the rear of the door and the problem is no more.<P>I'm not sure if the clips in that area were originally shorter than the others; if they were, they had been replaced or were mixed up by someone.<P>Actually, this problem was one of the reasons I got my car as cheap as I did. And thankfully the fix was simple.||||reg||10
Z||000002||mutfish||01-07-2000||06:24 PM||||That happend to me also......turned out to be the door lock solenoid wire was in the wrong place at the wrong time.....||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ed||01-08-2000||06:24 PM||||I clipped off the tips of the corner fasteners and fixed the problem. <P>Working on your own car is SO rewarding, and the joy of discovery, so sublime. ||||reg||14
